Author: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 14 15:44:12 2026 -0700

    Never change a nozzle while the printer's unsaved edits exist nowhere else

    A nozzle change on the project's printer drops the project copy's unsaved
    edits. It now runs only after a step the caller supplies has saved them to
    the project's version history; without that step, or when it fails, the
    nozzle stays and the person is told why. The printer panel supplies the
    autosave version as that step. Harness checks cover all three cases.

diff --git a/agent-docs/jusprin/mcp-tool-extension-guide.md b/agent-docs/jusprin/mcp-tool-extension-guide.md
